  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added an authentic Linux-only PARI 2.17.4 prepared-nf Outcome-C adapter. The helper prepares nfinit before the worker clock, resets PARI's stack and RNG for each run, times the complete bnfinit flag-zero class/unit root, emits implementation-neutral result/RNG/work evidence, and binds every timed result to an independent fresh-process replay. The shared worker now supports a fail-closed whole-root-only stage mode without manufacturing exclusive stages.",
    "risks": [
      "PARI's public bnfinit API has no audited internal stage callbacks, so all elapsed time is honestly assigned to the unattributed remainder and named stages remain zero.",
      "PARI flag zero does not materialize expanded fundamental units; the standardized result carries the exact rank, log matrix, regulator, and torsion but leaves expandedFundamentalUnits null.",
      "This benchmark reference is intentionally Linux-only and GPL-attributed; it is not product implementation.",
      "The portable suite fails in the unchanged modular-qexp source-freeze test: its committed manifest records acf5c55b... for architecture/package-graph.json while the unchanged file and exact base commit hash to 66d0eec3.... No unrelated modular-forms fixture was changed."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Implement or integrate the authentic Sage h=1 adapter against the same result, replay, RNG, and work contract.",
      "Have the paired coordinator run at least seven alternating pairs before setting finalTimingRun; this lane deliberately performs no final timing run.",
      "Either add audited PARI internal stage hooks or review a whole-root paired receipt schema before claiming named-stage attribution."
    ]
  }
